PRJECT FILE- Simple Network Configuration (Cisco Packet Tracer)
Project Title : Simple Network Configuration - Subnetting Exercise 
Objectives:
To design a small office network for two departments (Accounts and Delivery),
Subnet a given IP block, assign static IP addresses to all devices, and 
verify conectivity using ping

Base network: 192.168.40.0/24
subnetting 
Accounts Department:
192.168.40.0/25 (192.168.40.1- 192.168.40.126)
Delivery department:
192.168.40.128/25(192.168.40.129- 192.168.40.254)\

Devices per department 
-2pcs 
-1 printer 
-1 switches (connects department devices)
-Shared Router (Connects both departments)

Configuration steps 
1. Subnetted 192.168.40.0/24 into two /25 subnets for Accounts and Delivery 
2. Assgned static IPs, subnet masks, and default gateways to all PCs and printers 
3. Connected department devices to their respective switch
4. Connected both switches to the router 
5.Configured router interfaces with gateway IPs for each department subnet
6. Tested  conectivity with ping - within department and accross department 

Testin results:
-ping within same department: Succesful
-ping accross departments (Accounts <-> Delivery): Succesful
Tools used 
-- Cisco Packet Tracer 
